},
{
  n:7, level:3,
  title:'Augmented renal clearance after polytrauma',
  age:24, sex:'M', tbw:85, heightIn:72, scr:0.8,
  vignette:`<p>A 24-year-old man is in the surgical ICU on day 6 after a motorcycle collision with
    multiple long-bone fractures and a splenectomy. He develops a ventilator-associated pneumonia
    with MRSA in a bronchoalveolar lavage and one positive blood culture.</p>
    <p>Creatinine is 0.8 mg/dL. A measured 8-hour urine collection yesterday showed a creatinine
    clearance of 172 mL/min. He is on no vasopressors and no nephrotoxins.</p>`,
  crclNote:'The measured 8-hour collection corroborates this estimate. The augmented renal clearance here is real, not a laboratory artefact.',
  loading:{required:true, note:'Critically ill with MRSA bacteremia and pneumonia.'},
  maintenance:{mode:'auc', idealText:'1,250 mg IV q8h (total daily dose 3,750 mg). 1,000 mg q8h is the conservative end of the acceptable range.'},
  intervals:{full:['8','ci'], partial:['12'], note:'Shorten the interval rather than enlarging single doses. Continuous infusion is a legitimate alternative in augmented clearance.'},
  monitoring:{methodsFull:['auc_bayes','auc_2level'], timingFull:['early'], timingPartial:['ss'],
    idealText:'Early AUC-guided levels, and repeat them as he recovers &mdash; augmented clearance recedes, and the regimen that fits today can be too much next week.'},
  reasoning:`<ol>
    <li>Young, previously healthy, post-trauma, no renal disease: the classic augmented renal
    clearance phenotype. The measured collection at 172 mL/min corroborates the estimate.</li>
    <li>Loading dose 25 &times; 85 &asymp; <b>2,125 mg</b>, round to 2,000&ndash;2,250 mg.</li>
    <li>Clearance = 0.689(156) + 3.66 &asymp; 111 mL/min = 6.7 L/h. Target AUC 500 &rarr; about
    3,340 mg/day.</li>
    <li>Delivering that as 1,750 mg q12h means very high peaks; delivering it as
    <b>1,250 mg q8h</b> keeps concentrations steadier. Continuous infusion is the other reasonable
    answer at this clearance.</li>
    <li>A total daily dose near 3,750 mg is approaching the 4 g mark at which nephrotoxicity risk
    rises, so creatinine monitoring here is not optional.</li></ol>`,
  pattern:`Augmented renal clearance is where under-dosing hides, because the creatinine looks perfect. Any young trauma, burn, febrile neutropenic, or early-sepsis patient with a creatinine under 1.0 deserves a deliberate thought about whether their clearance is above normal &mdash; and the correction is a shorter interval, not a bigger dose.`,
  errors:[
    {when:(e,c)=>e.aucEst>0 && e.aucEst<c.aucPartialLo, msg:'This regimen leaves him substantially under-exposed. Sub-target vancomycin in MRSA bacteremia risks persistent bacteremia and selects for reduced susceptibility.'},
    {when:(e,c)=>e.md && e.md>2000, msg:'Single doses above about 2,000 mg mean long infusion times and high peaks. At augmented clearance, divide the daily dose into more frequent administrations instead.'}
  ]
},
{
