  pattern:`Severe renal impairment changes the interval and the total daily dose. It does not change the loading dose, and it does not change the target AUC of 400 to 600. Ask yourself which of the three you are actually adjusting before you write the order.`,
  errors:[
    {when:(e,c)=>e.ld===0, msg:'No loading dose was given. In advanced renal impairment the loading dose matters <i>more</i>, not less: without it, a patient clearing 0.9 L/h takes several days to reach target on maintenance dosing alone, and that is several days of sub-therapeutic bacteremia.'},
    {when:(e,c)=>e.ld>0 && e.ld/c.tbw < 18, msg:'Your loading dose is below 18 mg/kg of actual body weight. That looks like a reduction made for his kidneys. Volume of distribution is unchanged in renal failure.'},
