    kidney injury signal.</li>
    <li>The dose itself is ordinary arithmetic: adjusted body weight 63.2 kg, CrCl &asymp; 27 mL/min,
    clearance &asymp; 1.3 L/h, target AUC 500 &rarr; about 660 mg/day &rarr; <b>1,000 mg q36h or
    750 mg q24h</b>. Load 25 &times; 76 &asymp; <b>1,900 mg</b>.</li>
    <li>The tension is not resolved by picking a number between the two pressures. It is resolved
    by removing the modifiable risk: <b>the piperacillin-tazobactam is the thing to change.</b> Now
    that the gram-negative organism is identified, narrow it &mdash; to cefepime, a carbapenem, or
    whatever susceptibilities allow. That subtracts a nephrotoxicity risk factor without
    subtracting any antimicrobial coverage.</li>
    <li>Then aim squarely at the middle of 400&ndash;600 rather than shading low out of anxiety, and
    measure early instead of at steady state.</li>
    <li>Also legitimate to raise: linezolid penetrates the central nervous system well and is not
    nephrotoxic, so it is a genuine alternative for an epidural abscess in a patient whose kidneys
    are declining. Daptomycin would be a poorer fit here.</li></ol>`,
  pattern:`When two priorities pull in opposite directions, the useful move is rarely to split the difference in the dose. Look for the third variable &mdash; the companion antibiotic, the line, the source, the alternative agent &mdash; that lets you stop trading one risk against the other. Splitting the difference usually means under-treating the infection <i>and</i> keeping the nephrotoxicity.`,
  errors:[
    {when:(e,c)=>e.aucEst>0 && e.aucEst<c.aucFullLo, msg:'You shaded the dose low, presumably out of concern for her kidneys. That leaves an epidural abscess under-treated while the vancomycin plus piperacillin-tazobactam combination continues unchanged &mdash; the risk was not actually reduced, only the efficacy was.'},
    {when:(e,c)=>e.timing==='ss', msg:'With a creatinine already drifting up on two agents, waiting until steady state gives up the early warning you most want here.'}
  ]
}
];

/* ==================================================================================
   SECTION 4 — GRADING ENGINE
   Tolerance-based, never exact-match. Each component is scored independently so the
   learner can see, for example, that their dose was right and their interval was not.
   ================================================================================== */

/* Points are spread across the four things the learner actually decides. */
const DEFAULT_WEIGHTS = {ld:25, maint:40, interval:15, monitor:20};

const INTERVAL_LABELS = {
  '8':'every 8 hours','12':'every 12 hours','24':'every 24 hours','36':'every 36 hours',
  '48':'every 48 hours','72':'every 72 hours','ci':'continuous infusion',
  'posthd':'after each hemodialysis session','bylevel':'hold and redose by level'
};
const METHOD_LABELS = {
  auc_bayes:'AUC-guided, Bayesian estimate from a single level',
  auc_2level:'AUC-guided, peak and trough with first-order equations',
  trough_1520:'Trough only, target 15\u201320 mg/L',
  trough_1015:'Trough only, target 10\u201315 mg/L',
  peak_only:'Peak level only',
  none:'No routine level monitoring'
};
const TIMING_LABELS = {
  early:'Early \u2014 within roughly the first 24 hours, before steady state',
  ss:'At steady state \u2014 around the fourth dose',
  prehd:'Before a hemodialysis session',
  weekly:'Weekly only',
  none:'No scheduled level'
};

/* Everything derived from a case. Kept as one object so grading and feedback read from
   the same numbers the reasoning text quotes. */
function buildContext(c){
  const ibwVal = ibw(c.heightIn, c.sex);
  const adjVal = adjbw(c.tbw, c.heightIn, c.sex);
  const sel    = cgWeight(c.tbw, c.heightIn, c.sex);
  const ctx = {
    tbw:c.tbw, ibwVal, adjVal, cgWeightUsed:sel.w, cgWeightWhich:sel.which,
    bmi:+(c.tbw / Math.pow(c.heightIn*0.0254, 2)).toFixed(1),
    crclCG:     cockcroftGault(c.age, c.sex, sel.w, c.scr)
  };
  /* crclForAuc drives both the AUC model and the accumulation safety check. Set it to 0
     when no clearance estimate is meaningful (dialysis, CRRT) so neither one fires. */
  ctx.crclForAuc = (c.crclForAuc != null) ? c.crclForAuc
                 : (c.crclApplicable === false ? 0 : ctx.crclCG);
  const af = c.aucFull    || [DOSING_ASSUMPTIONS.aucTargetLow, DOSING_ASSUMPTIONS.aucTargetHigh];
  const ap = c.aucPartial || [340, 700];
  ctx.aucFullLo = af[0]; ctx.aucFullHi = af[1];
  ctx.aucPartialLo = ap[0]; ctx.aucPartialHi = ap[1];

  // Loading dose acceptance window, in mg, on ACTUAL body weight, honouring the cap.
  const lo = (c.loading.mgkgLow  != null) ? c.loading.mgkgLow  : DOSING_ASSUMPTIONS.loadingMgKgLow;
  const hi = (c.loading.mgkgHigh != null) ? c.loading.mgkgHigh : DOSING_ASSUMPTIONS.loadingMgKgHigh;
  const cap = DOSING_ASSUMPTIONS.loadingCapMg;
  ctx.ldFullLo = Math.min(lo * c.tbw, cap * 0.8);
  ctx.ldFullHi = Math.min(hi * c.tbw, cap);
  ctx.ldIdeal  = round250(Math.min(DOSING_ASSUMPTIONS.loadingMgKgTarget * c.tbw, cap));
  ctx.weights  = c.weights || DEFAULT_WEIGHTS;
  return ctx;
}

/* Read the form into a normalised entry object. */
function readEntries(c, ctx){
  const num = id => { const v = document.getElementById(id); return v && v.value !== '' ? Number(v.value) : null; };
  const e = {
    ld:   num('inLd'),
    md:   num('inMd'),
    interval: document.getElementById('inInterval').value,
    method:   document.getElementById('inMethod').value,
    timing:   document.getElementById('inTiming').value
  };
  e.tdd = (e.md != null) ? tddFrom(e.md, e.interval) : null;
  e.mdPerDay = e.tdd;
  // Only model AUC where a population clearance estimate is defensible.
  e.aucEst = (c.maintenance.mode === 'auc' && e.tdd != null && ctx.crclForAuc > 0)
    ? estimateAUC(e.tdd, ctx.crclForAuc) : 0;
  return e;
}

/* --- component graders. Each returns {status:'ok'|'part'|'miss', pts, said, note} --- */

function gradeLoading(c, ctx, e, max){
  const mgkg = e.ld > 0 ? +(e.ld / c.tbw).toFixed(1) : 0;
  let status, note;
  if (e.ld === 0){
    status = c.loading.required ? 'miss' : 'ok';
    note = c.loading.required
      ? `A loading dose was indicated here. Target about ${ctx.ldIdeal} mg (${DOSING_ASSUMPTIONS.loadingMgKgTarget} mg/kg of actual body weight, capped at ${DOSING_ASSUMPTIONS.loadingCapMg} mg).`
      : 'No loading dose was required in this case.';
  } else if (e.ld > DOSING_ASSUMPTIONS.loadingCapMg){
    status = 'part';
    note = `Above the ${DOSING_ASSUMPTIONS.loadingCapMg} mg cap used in this trainer. Caps of 2,000\u20133,000 mg are both in institutional use \u2014 know which one applies where you practise.`;
  } else if (e.ld >= ctx.ldFullLo && e.ld <= ctx.ldFullHi){
    status = 'ok';
    note = `${mgkg} mg/kg of actual body weight, inside the acceptable window of about ${Math.round(ctx.ldFullLo)}\u2013${Math.round(ctx.ldFullHi)} mg. ${c.loading.note}`;
  } else if (e.ld >= ctx.ldFullLo*0.85 && e.ld <= ctx.ldFullHi*1.15){
    status = 'part';
    note = `${mgkg} mg/kg of actual body weight \u2014 just outside the window of about ${Math.round(ctx.ldFullLo)}\u2013${Math.round(ctx.ldFullHi)} mg.`;
  } else {
    status = 'miss';
    note = `${mgkg} mg/kg of actual body weight. The acceptable window here is about ${Math.round(ctx.ldFullLo)}\u2013${Math.round(ctx.ldFullHi)} mg (target ${ctx.ldIdeal} mg). ${c.loading.note}`;
  }
  return {status, pts: status==='ok'?max:status==='part'?Math.round(max*0.5):0,
          said: e.ld === 0 ? 'You gave no loading dose.' : `You gave ${e.ld} mg.`, note};
}

function gradeMaintenance(c, ctx, e, max){
  const m = c.maintenance;
  const half = Math.round(max*0.5);

  // A level-guided plan is the intended answer in cases that say so.
  if (e.interval === 'bylevel'){
    if (m.levelGuidedOk) return {status:'ok', pts:max, said:'You held scheduled maintenance and planned to redose by level.',
      note:`That is a correct answer here. ${m.idealText}`};
    return {status:'miss', pts:0, said:'You held scheduled maintenance and planned to redose by level.',
      note:`Renal function is stable enough in this patient to write a schedule. ${m.idealText}`};
  }

  if (m.mode === 'mgkgdose'){
    const mgkg = +(e.md / c.tbw).toFixed(1);
    const inFull = mgkg >= m.full[0] && mgkg <= m.full[1];
    const inPart = mgkg >= m.partial[0] && mgkg <= m.partial[1];
    const status = inFull ? 'ok' : inPart ? 'part' : 'miss';
    return {status, pts: inFull?max:inPart?half:0, said:`You gave ${e.md} mg per dose (${mgkg} mg/kg of actual body weight).`,
      note:`The supplemental dose here should be about ${m.full[0]}\u2013${m.full[1]} mg/kg. ${m.idealText}`};
  }

  if (m.mode === 'mgkgday'){
    if (e.tdd == null) return {status:'miss', pts:0, said:'No total daily dose could be worked out from your interval.',
      note:`${m.idealText}`};
    const mgkgd = +(e.tdd / c.tbw).toFixed(1);
    const inFull = mgkgd >= m.full[0] && mgkgd <= m.full[1];
    const inPart = mgkgd >= m.partial[0] && mgkgd <= m.partial[1];
    const status = inFull ? 'ok' : inPart ? 'part' : 'miss';
    return {status, pts: inFull?max:inPart?half:0,
      said:`Your regimen delivers ${e.tdd} mg/day (${mgkgd} mg/kg/day).`,
      note:`On CRRT the target is about ${m.full[0]}\u2013${m.full[1]} mg/kg/day. ${m.idealText}`};
  }

  // Default: AUC-based grading.
  if (e.tdd == null) return {status:'miss', pts:0,
    said:'Your interval choice does not produce a scheduled daily dose.',
    note:`${m.idealText}`};
  const a = e.aucEst;
  const inFull = a >= ctx.aucFullLo && a <= ctx.aucFullHi;
  const inPart = a >= ctx.aucPartialLo && a <= ctx.aucPartialHi;
  const status = inFull ? 'ok' : inPart ? 'part' : 'miss';
  return {status, pts: inFull?max:inPart?half:0,
    said:`${e.md} mg ${INTERVAL_LABELS[e.interval]} delivers ${e.tdd} mg/day, an estimated AUC\u2082\u2084 of about ${a} mg\u00b7h/L.`,
    note:`Target is ${ctx.aucFullLo}\u2013${ctx.aucFullHi}. ${m.idealText}`};
}

function gradeInterval(c, ctx, e, max){
  const iv = c.intervals;
  const status = iv.full.includes(e.interval) ? 'ok'
               : (iv.partial||[]).includes(e.interval) ? 'part' : 'miss';
  return {status, pts: status==='ok'?max:status==='part'?Math.round(max*0.5):0,
    said:`You chose ${INTERVAL_LABELS[e.interval]}.`,
    note:`${iv.note} Full credit here: ${iv.full.map(x=>INTERVAL_LABELS[x]).join(', or ')}.`};
}

function gradeMonitoring(c, ctx, e, max){
  const mo = c.monitoring;
  const halfMax = Math.round(max/2), restMax = max - halfMax;
  const mStat = mo.methodsFull.includes(e.method) ? 'ok'
              : (mo.methodsPartial||[]).includes(e.method) ? 'part' : 'miss';
  const tFull = mo.timingFull || ['ss','early'];
  const tStat = tFull.includes(e.timing) ? 'ok'
              : (mo.timingPartial||[]).includes(e.timing) ? 'part' : 'miss';
  const pts = (mStat==='ok'?halfMax:mStat==='part'?Math.round(halfMax/2):0)
            + (tStat==='ok'?restMax:tStat==='part'?Math.round(restMax/2):0);
  const status = (mStat==='ok'&&tStat==='ok') ? 'ok' : pts>0 ? 'part' : 'miss';
  return {status, pts,
    said:`You chose: ${METHOD_LABELS[e.method]}, drawn ${TIMING_LABELS[e.timing].toLowerCase()}.`,
    note:mo.idealText};
}

/* Safety review runs independently of scoring: a regimen can be "close enough" on points
   and still be something you would not let leave the pharmacy. */
function safetyReview(c, ctx, e){
  const flags = [];
  const A = DOSING_ASSUMPTIONS;
  if (e.ld > A.loadingCapMg)
    flags.push(`Loading dose of ${e.ld} mg exceeds the ${A.loadingCapMg} mg cap used here. Above this, infusion-related reactions and phlebitis rise without added benefit.`);
  if (e.tdd && e.tdd > A.maxTotalDailyMg)
    flags.push(`Total daily dose of ${e.tdd} mg is above the ${A.maxTotalDailyMg} mg/day ceiling. Daily doses at or above 4 g are an independent risk factor for acute kidney injury.`);
  if (e.md && e.md > A.maxSingleMaintenanceMg && e.interval !== 'ci')
    flags.push(`Single maintenance dose of ${e.md} mg is above ${A.maxSingleMaintenanceMg} mg. Doses this large require prolonged infusion and produce high peaks; divide the daily dose instead.`);
  if (e.aucEst >= 1000)
    flags.push(`Estimated AUC\u2082\u2084 of about ${e.aucEst} mg\u00b7h/L is grossly supratherapeutic \u2014 roughly double the upper limit. This is a patient-harm regimen, not a near miss.`);
  else if (e.aucEst > 700)
    flags.push(`Estimated AUC\u2082\u2084 of about ${e.aucEst} mg\u00b7h/L is well above the ${A.aucNephroThreshold} threshold associated with nephrotoxicity.`);
  if (e.aucEst > 0 && e.aucEst < 300)
    flags.push(`Estimated AUC\u2082\u2084 of about ${e.aucEst} mg\u00b7h/L is substantially sub-therapeutic. In MRSA bacteremia this risks persistent infection and selects for reduced vancomycin susceptibility \u2014 under-dosing is a safety issue, not a conservative choice.`);
  if (['8','12'].includes(e.interval) && ctx.crclForAuc > 0 && ctx.crclForAuc < 30)
    flags.push(`An interval of ${INTERVAL_LABELS[e.interval]} at an estimated clearance near ${ctx.crclForAuc} mL/min will accumulate over successive doses even if the first dose looks reasonable.`);
  if (e.ld === 0 && c.loading.required)
    flags.push('No loading dose in a serious infection means several days at sub-therapeutic concentrations while maintenance dosing slowly accumulates.');
  if (e.method === 'none')
    flags.push('No monitoring plan. Vancomycin has a narrow therapeutic window and appreciable interpatient variability; a regimen without levels is a guess that never gets checked.');
  return flags;
}

function gradeCase(c, ctx, e){
  const w = ctx.weights;
  const rows = [];
  rows.push(Object.assign({name:'Loading dose'},        gradeLoading(c,ctx,e,w.ld),       {max:w.ld}));
  rows.push(Object.assign({name:'Maintenance dose'},    gradeMaintenance(c,ctx,e,w.maint),{max:w.maint}));
  rows.push(Object.assign({name:'Interval'},            gradeInterval(c,ctx,e,w.interval),{max:w.interval}));
  rows.push(Object.assign({name:'Monitoring plan'},     gradeMonitoring(c,ctx,e,w.monitor),{max:w.monitor}));
  const total = rows.reduce((s,r)=>s+r.pts, 0);
  const errs = (c.errors||[]).filter(x=>{ try { return x.when(e, Object.assign({}, ctx, {tbw:c.tbw})); } catch(_){ return false; } });
  return {rows, total, flags:safetyReview(c,ctx,e), errs};
}

/* ==================================================================================
   SECTION 5 — INTERFACE
   In-memory state only. No localStorage or sessionStorage anywhere in this file.
   ================================================================================== */

const state = { i:0, results:[], submitted:false };
const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);
const esc = s => String(s).replace(/[&<>"]/g, m => ({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;'}[m]));

function renderPrimer(){
  $('primerContent').innerHTML = PRIMER.map(p => `
    <details class="primer"${p.open ? ' open' : ''}>
      <summary>${p.title}</summary>
      <div class="primer-body">${p.html}</div>
    </details>`).join('');
}

function renderChrome(){
  $('statCase').textContent = Math.min(state.i + 1, CASES.length) + '/' + CASES.length;
  const done = state.results.length;
  if (done === 0) { $('statScore').textContent = '\u2014'; }
  else {
    const pct = Math.round(state.results.reduce((s,r)=>s+r.total,0) / done);
    $('statScore').textContent = pct + '%';
  }
  $('trackbar').innerHTML = CASES.map((_,k) =>
    `<i class="${k < state.results.length ? 'done' : k === state.i ? 'now' : ''}"></i>`).join('');
}

function opt(map, list){ return list.map(k=>`<option value="${k}">${map[k]}</option>`).join(''); }

function renderCase(){
  const c = CASES[state.i];
  const ctx = buildContext(c);
  state.ctx = ctx;
  state.submitted = false;

  const showCrcl = c.crclApplicable !== false;
  const isObese  = c.tbw >= 1.25 * ctx.ibwVal;
  const heightFt = Math.floor(c.heightIn/12) + "'" + (c.heightIn % 12) + '"';

  $('stage').innerHTML = `
  <section class="card">
    <div class="case-head">
      <span class="case-no">CASE ${String(c.n).padStart(2,'0')} OF ${CASES.length}</span>
      <h2 class="case-title">${esc(c.title)}</h2>
      <span class="chip l${c.level}">${LEVELS[c.level]}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="case-grid">
      <div class="vignette">${c.vignette}</div>
      <div class="flowsheet">
        <h3>At a glance</h3>
        <dl>
          <div class="row"><dt>Age</dt><dd>${c.age} y</dd></div>
          <div class="row"><dt>Sex</dt><dd>${c.sex === 'F' ? 'female' : 'male'}</dd></div>
          <div class="row"><dt>Weight</dt><dd>${c.tbw} kg</dd></div>
          <div class="row"><dt>Height</dt><dd>${heightFt} (${c.heightIn} in)</dd></div>
          <div class="row${c.scr >= 2 ? ' alert' : ''}"><dt>Creatinine</dt><dd>${c.scr} mg/dL</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <h3 class="sub">Calculated for you</h3>
        <dl>
          <div class="row calc"><dt>Ideal body weight</dt><dd>${ctx.ibwVal} kg</dd></div>
          ${isObese ? `<div class="row calc"><dt>Adjusted body weight</dt><dd>${ctx.adjVal} kg</dd></div>` : ''}
          <div class="row calc"><dt>CrCl (Cockcroft-Gault)</dt>
            <dd>${showCrcl ? ctx.crclCG + ' mL/min' : 'n/a'}</dd></div>
        </dl>
        ${showCrcl ? `<div class="via">Calculated using ${ctx.cgWeightWhich} (${ctx.cgWeightUsed} kg), which is ${Math.round(100*c.tbw/ctx.ibwVal)}% of ideal.</div>` : ''}
        ${c.crclNote ? `<div class="flag">${c.crclNote}</div>` : ''}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Write the regimen</h2>
    <div class="card-body">
      <div class="form-grid">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="inLd">Loading dose</label>
          <div class="unit-wrap"><input type="number" id="inLd" min="0" max="6000" step="50" inputmode="numeric"><span class="unit">mg</span></div>
          <div class="hint">Enter 0 if you would not give one.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="inMd">Maintenance dose</label>
          <div class="unit-wrap"><input type="number" id="inMd" min="0" max="6000" step="50" inputmode="numeric"><span class="unit">mg</span></div>
          <div class="hint">Per dose. For continuous infusion, enter the 24-hour total.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="inInterval">Interval</label>
          <select id="inInterval">
            <option value="">Choose an interval</option>
            ${opt(INTERVAL_LABELS, ['8','12','24','36','48','72','ci','posthd','bylevel'])}
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="inMethod">Monitoring method</label>
          <select id="inMethod">
            <option value="">Choose a method</option>
            ${opt(METHOD_LABELS, ['auc_bayes','auc_2level','trough_1520','trough_1015','peak_only','none'])}
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="inTiming">When do you draw the level</label>
          <select id="inTiming">
            <option value="">Choose a time</option>
            ${opt(TIMING_LABELS, ['early','ss','prehd','weekly','none'])}
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <button id="btnCheck">Check my regimen</button>
        <span class="validation" id="valMsg"></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div id="fbSlot"></div>`;

  $('btnCheck').addEventListener('click', onCheck);
  renderChrome();
  if (window.scrollTo) window.scrollTo({top:0, behavior:'smooth'});
}

function validate(c, e){
  if (e.ld === null) return 'Enter a loading dose, or 0 if you would not give one.';
  if (e.md === null || e.md <= 0) return 'Enter a maintenance dose greater than 0.';
  if (!e.interval) return 'Choose an interval.';
  if (!e.method) return 'Choose a monitoring method.';
  if (!e.timing) return 'Choose when the level is drawn.';
  if (e.md > 6000 || e.ld > 6000) return 'That dose is outside any plausible range. Check the value before submitting.';
  return null;
}

function onCheck(){
  if (state.submitted) return;
  const c = CASES[state.i], ctx = state.ctx;
  const e = readEntries(c, ctx);
  const problem = validate(c, e);
  $('valMsg').textContent = problem || '';
  if (problem) return;

  state.submitted = true;
  const g = gradeCase(c, ctx, e);
  state.results.push({ n:c.n, title:c.title, total:g.total, rows:g.rows.map(r=>({name:r.name, pts:r.pts, max:r.max})) });
  $('btnCheck').disabled = true;
  $('btnCheck').textContent = 'Submitted';
  ['inLd','inMd','inInterval','inMethod','inTiming'].forEach(id=>{ const el=$(id); if(el) el.disabled = true; });
  renderFeedback(c, ctx, e, g);
  renderChrome();
}

function verdictLabel(total, flagCount){
  // Points are additive and a regimen can lose only a few of them and still be unsafe, so
  // the headline is driven by the safety review first and the score second.
  if (flagCount) return flagCount === 1
    ? 'Scored, but the safety review below found a problem.'
    : `Scored, but the safety review below found ${flagCount} problems.`;
  if (total >= 85) return 'A regimen you could sign.';
  if (total >= 65) return 'Broadly reasonable, with something to fix.';
  if (total >= 40) return 'Partly there. Work through the reasoning below.';
  return 'Rebuild this one from the six-step approach.';
}

function ruler(auc, lo, hi){
  const SCALE = 1000;
  const pos = Math.min(auc / SCALE, 1) * 100;
  return `
  <div class="ruler-block">
    <div class="ruler-head"><span>Estimated 24-hour exposure from your regimen</span>
      <b>AUC\u2082\u2084 \u2248 ${auc} mg\u00b7h/L</b></div>
    <div class="ruler">
      <div class="band" style="left:${lo/SCALE*100}%;width:${(hi-lo)/SCALE*100}%"></div>
      <div class="marker" data-v="${auc}" style="left:${pos}%"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ruler-scale"><span>0</span><span>250</span><span>500</span><span>750</span><span>1000+</span></div>
  </div>`;
}

function renderFeedback(c, ctx, e, g){
  const showRuler = c.maintenance.mode === 'auc' && e.tdd != null && e.aucEst > 0;
  const html = `
  <section class="card fb">
    <h2>Feedback \u2014 case ${String(c.n).padStart(2,'0')}</h2>
    <div class="verdict">
      <span class="score">${g.total}<small>/100</small></span>
      <span class="label">${verdictLabel(g.total, g.flags.length)}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      ${g.flags.length ? `<div class="safety"><h4>Safety review</h4><ul>${g.flags.map(f=>`<li>${f}</li>`).join('')}</ul></div>` : ''}
      ${showRuler ? ruler(e.aucEst, ctx.aucFullLo, ctx.aucFullHi) : ''}

      <table class="breakdown">
        <tr><th>Component</th><th style="text-align:right">Points</th></tr>
        ${g.rows.map(r=>`
          <tr class="${r.status}">
            <td><span class="mark">${r.status==='ok'?'\u2713':r.status==='part'?'\u2248':'\u2715'}</span>
              <b>${r.name}</b>
              <span class="yours">${r.said}</span>
              <span class="yours">${r.note}</span></td>
            <td class="pts">${r.pts}/${r.max}</td>
          </tr>`).join('')}
      </table>

      <div class="section-h">How a clinician gets there</div>
      <div class="reasoning">${c.reasoning}</div>

      ${g.errs.length ? `
      <div class="diag"><h4>Where your answer most likely came from</h4>
        <ul>${g.errs.map(x=>`<li>${x.msg}</li>`).join('')}</ul></div>` : ''}

      <div class="section-h">Carry this forward</div>
      <div class="pattern"><h4>The transferable rule</h4>${c.pattern}</div>

      <div class="actions">
        <button id="btnNext">${state.i === CASES.length-1 ? 'See session summary' : 'Next case'}</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>`;
  $('fbSlot').innerHTML = html;
  $('btnNext').addEventListener('click', ()=>{
    state.i++;
    if (state.i >= CASES.length) renderSummary(); else renderCase();
  });
  const slot = $('fbSlot');
  if (slot.scrollIntoView) slot.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth', block:'start'});
}

function renderSummary(){
  const r = state.results;
  const overall = Math.round(r.reduce((s,x)=>s+x.total,0)/r.length);
  const firstHalf = r.slice(0, Math.ceil(r.length/2));
  const secondHalf = r.slice(Math.ceil(r.length/2));
  const avg = a => Math.round(a.reduce((s,x)=>s+x.total,0)/a.length);

  // Aggregate by component so the learner sees which step of the approach is weak,
  // rather than only which cases went badly.
  const agg = {};
  r.forEach(x => x.rows.forEach(row => {
    agg[row.name] = agg[row.name] || {pts:0, max:0};
    agg[row.name].pts += row.pts; agg[row.name].max += row.max;
  }));
  const weakest = Object.entries(agg)
    .map(([k,v])=>({k, pct: Math.round(100*v.pts/v.max)}))
    .sort((a,b)=>a.pct-b.pct);

  $('stage').innerHTML = `
  <section class="card fb">
    <h2>Session summary</h2>
    <div class="card-body">
      <div class="summary-grid">
        <div><div class="big">${overall}<small>/100</small></div><div class="stat" style="margin-top:2px">Overall</div></div>
        <div><div class="big">${avg(firstHalf)}<small>&nbsp;\u2192&nbsp;${avg(secondHalf)}</small></div><div class="stat" style="margin-top:2px">First half \u2192 second half</div></div>
        <div><div class="big">${r.length}</div><div class="stat" style="margin-top:2px">Cases completed</div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="section-h">Score by case</div>
      <div class="spark-wrap"><div class="spark">
        ${r.map(x=>`<div class="b" style="height:${Math.max(4, x.total)}%" title="Case ${x.n}: ${x.total}/100"><b>${x.n}</b></div>`).join('')}
      </div></div>

      <div class="section-h">By step of the approach</div>
      <table class="breakdown">
        ${weakest.map(w=>`<tr class="${w.pct>=80?'ok':w.pct>=55?'part':'miss'}">
          <td><span class="mark">${w.pct>=80?'\u2713':w.pct>=55?'\u2248':'\u2715'}</span><b>${w.k}</b></td>
          <td class="pts">${w.pct}%</td></tr>`).join('')}
      </table>
      <div class="pattern" style="margin-top:16px"><h4>Where to concentrate next</h4>
        The lowest-scoring component above is <b>${weakest[0].k.toLowerCase()}</b>. Re-read that section
        of the reference panel, then run the cases again \u2014 the scenarios stay the same, so the point is
        whether the reasoning arrives faster and lands more often, not whether you remember the numbers.
      </div>

      <div class="actions"><button id="btnRestart">Start a new session</button></div>
    </div>
  </section>`;
  $('btnRestart').addEventListener('click', ()=>{
    state.i = 0; state.results = []; state.submitted = false;
    renderCase();
  });
  renderChrome();
  if (window.scrollTo) window.scrollTo({top:0, behavior:'smooth'});
}

renderPrimer();
renderCase();
</script>
</body>
</html>
